WHAT IS AND IS NOT COVERED BY THAT LICENCE
------------------------------------------
Apache-2.0 covers the material this project authored: the case definitions
(case.json), the established ground truth (ground-truth.json), the build
recipes (Dockerfile, clone.sh, build.sh, link.sh), the test application
sources, the scorer (score.py), the harness (run.py) and the documentation.

The corpus also contains BUILD OUTPUTS -- linker maps, compilation databases,
size listings and digests -- produced by compiling third-party open-source
projects. Those projects carry their own upstream licences, recorded per case
in case.json:

    Mbed TLS                 Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later
    FreeRTOS-Plus-TCP        MIT
    FreeRTOS kernel          MIT
    newlib                   BSD-like, several licences

A linker map is an artefact of a build, not a copy of a project's source. It
carries symbol names, object file names and byte counts. It is published here
so that the ground truth can be independently checked, which is the only way a
benchmark means anything.

No third-party source code is redistributed here. Each case's clone.sh fetches
upstream at a pinned tag, so anybody can reproduce the build rather than take
these figures on trust.
